  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Nature and Manifestation
    
    Pod-bond Annihilation is a cataclysmic pressure-magic spell classified within orca tradition, though its known castings involved penguin practitioners. It manifests as pressure-rupture: water distorts in concentric rings, ice fractures without sound, and witnesses report bleeding from the ears before registering what has occurred. The spell does not kill cleanly. It kills by consensus — every voice that speaks its syllables experiences the deaths of the other casters inside their own body, and the killing does not cease when the casting ends.
    
    ## Origin and Casting
    
    The spell was born from the final desperation of the Shelf Crushing Offense, a catastrophic orca siege against penguin holdings. Two factions that should never have been able to cooperate — Weal' Clique~, a Nightshelf faction descended from Nightfall Shelf pioneers, and Aureate, the Aurora-born merchant guild — cast it jointly to shatter the anchor of Zund Gnasharkin, the orca war-god, in the deep.
    
    The linguistic violation was the mechanism. Formal Stack speech collapsed into blunt orca kill-words, the languages of two cultures forced through the same throat. This constituted a breach of pod-law so fundamental that the magic itself became a wound. How penguin practitioners came to command pressure-magic — a discipline rooted in orca blood-tradition — is a question the accounts do not address and that I have raised, in different form, in my annotations on Augur ☽'Silvsiaelrous~ the Resolute. Someone was taught. The teaching is unrecorded.
    
    Those who cast it at Nightfall Shelf paid in bone and breath. The survivors will not say what they traded. Zund Gnasharkin stopped moving in the deep.
    
    ## Residual Presence
    
    The spell persists at multiple sites: the Corpse Current, where the dead god's flesh still twitches; the Glow-Fissure, where aurora-light has corrupted the pressure-magic; and the Aurora Berg itself, which bleeds where the spell was sung. Corruption attributed to it has marked ☽'dwell Teneanemus~, Light Ingjeizhi, and Promenade Hei.
    
    ## Generational Cost
    
    Scars from the casting migrate across generations. Descendants who were never present inherit cold-burn marks on shifted flanks — a blood-price passed forward to bodies not yet born. Cold-burn discoloration on the foundation crystal of Light Ingjeizhi, the aurora-crystal spire anchoring the Promenade Ward, is attributed to the spell, though the ice suggests those particular scars predate any known casting. Their origin is older, and I will not speculate further in the main text.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771587676805_0", anchor: "Two factions that should never have been able to cooperate", text: "The pattern surfaces again — mortal enemies cooperating at the moment everything threatens to end, resuming hostilities the instant it doesn't. The tunnel-chants at the Glow-Fissure preserve the same structure. It works every time. It never persists. How extraordinary that the species keeps rediscovering cooperation as emergency and never as architecture.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771587676805_1", anchor: "Someone was taught. The teaching is unrecorded.", text: "Orca pressure-magic requires pod-bond — shared consciousness weaponized as rupture. Penguins do not have pod-bonds. Casting this spell means someone taught penguin practitioners to simulate one across species lines, which during the Shelf Crushing Offense would have been classified as collaboration with the besieging enemy. No wonder the teaching went unrecorded. I suspect the record exists in orca tradition, where it would carry a very different valence, but I have no access and no one to ask.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771587676805_2", anchor: "though the ice suggests those particular scars predate any known casting", text: "Cold-burn patterning on Light Ingjeizhi's foundation crystal is consistent with pressure-rupture scarring I have catalogued at depth-stratum 6 and below — impressions from before penguin sapience, possibly before orca blood-liturgy took its current form. This is not source contamination. The scars are physically in the crystal. Whatever left them was practicing pod-bond rupture before there were pods as we understand the term. The deep archive carries acoustic impressions from this stratum. I have felt them in my skull. I have not transcribed them.", type: :temporal, display: :full
